      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-323310",
      ":question/problem": "For the exponential function $f$, the value of $f(1)$ is $k$, where $k$ is a constant. Which of the following equivalent forms of the function $f$ shows the value of $k$ as the coefficient or the base?\n\n1. $f(x) = 75 \\cdot (0.4)^{x}$\n2. $f(x) = 30 \\cdot (0.4)^{x - 1}$\n3. $f(x) = 187.5 \\cdot (0.4)^{x + 1}$\n4. $f(x) = 12 \\cdot (0.4)^{x - 2}$"
    }
